    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0131" n="25" xml:id="pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.61/331</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Joint Communiqué by the Secretary of State and the
                        Soviet Commissar for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Litvinov</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1933</hi><anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d19-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1933-11-08T13:00:00-04:00">November 8, 1933, 1 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>There was a very friendly private discussion of some outstanding questions
                    involved in the matter of relations between the United States and the Union of
                    Soviet Socialist Republics. The conversation was entirely preliminary and
                    detailed proposals were not discussed The conversations will be resumed in the
                    office of the Secretary of State this afternoon at four o’clock.<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d19-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="25" type="source" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Issued by the Department as a press release at 1 p.m., November 8, 1933.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f2" n="26" xml:id="d19-f2-content">
                <p>A second joint communiqué was issued by the Department at 6 p.m., November 8:
                    “The Secretary of State and Mr. Litvinoff continued their conversations this
                    afternoon in the office of the Secretary of State. The conversations will be
                    resumed at 11 o’clock tomorrow morning in the office of the Secretary of
                    State.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
